From: Josh Hoffer <jhoffer@sansorgan.es>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:07:36 -0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH 4/4] Documentation: usb: describe dbc_net, the DbC network
 function

Describe the network function the previous patch adds:
- what it needs: USB_XHCI_DBGCAP_NET;
- the dbc_net parameter that picks it when ttyDBC is built too;
- the interfaces at both ends and its USB identity;
- the framing, for debug hosts without the dbcnet driver.

Note that the TTY function now needs USB_XHCI_DBGCAP_TTY, and give the
network function's default product ID in the ABI entry for
dbc_idProduct.

Written, with this changelog, by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI coding assistant.
See the cover letter for how it was made and tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
